'''''Shadow Games''''' is a novel by [[Michael Reaves]] and [[Maya Kaathryn Bohnhoff]] that was released on [[November 29]], [[2011]]. It is a "rags to riches" story of a [[holostar]] during the [[Alliance to Restore the Republic/Legends|Rebellion's]] early days, taking place in [[0 BBY/Legends|0 BBY]], before the events of [[Star Wars: Episode IV A New Hope|''Star Wars'': Episode IV ''A New Hope'']]. The short story "[[And Leebo Makes Three]]", also written by Reaves and Bohnhoff and published in [[Star Wars Insider 128|''Star Wars Insider'' 128]]<ref name="TERC" /> on [[September 13]], [[2011]],<ref name="Parent release date">[[Star Wars Insider 127|''Star Wars Insider'' 127]]</ref> serves as a prequel to the novel.<ref name="TERC" />

==Publisher's summary==
'''Some games are played for life or death.'''

''Javul Charn is the most famous pop star in the galaxy &ndash; and the runaway bride of a violent lieutenant in Black Sun, the crime syndicate commanded by Prince Xizor. Or so Javul says. Soon after Dash Rendar, broke and desperate, agrees to be Javul's bodyguard, he realizes that openness is not her strong suit &ndash; and that murder is stalking her tour. Between the discovery of dead bodies in a cargo hold and an attack by an unidentified warship, Dash and co-pilot Eaden Vrill desperately try to understand who is terrorizing Javul's tour and why. When Han Solo suddenly joins Javul's road show, the stakes are raised even higher. Now Dash, who has a history with Han and an even worse history with Prince Xizor, follows his instincts, his discoveries, and Javul herself &ndash; straight into a world that may be too dangerous to survive!''

