==Development==
''Shadows Games'' initially started as a novel entitled ''Holostar'' by [[Michael Reaves]] and [[Steve Perry]]. Perry and Reaves pitched the idea for ''Holostar'' around [[2007]] while discussing about making another ''[[Star Wars]]'' novel together. Perry himself came up with the basic premise of a story set in the entertainment industry, crafting the character of [[Javul Charn]]. However, [[Del Rey]] asked for some changes like including characters from the main ''Star Wars'' [[canon]]. Unwilling to make so, Perry and Reaves left and the project was shelved.<ref name="Perry Blog">{{Blogspot|subdomain=themanwhonevermissed|url=2012/01/star-wars-bookery.html|name=The Man Who Never Missed|text=Old Enough to Know Better: Star Wars Bookery|date=2012-01-29}}</ref>

A couple of years later, Del Rey had gotten more interested in the idea and offered Reaves and Perry to rehire them to write it albeit still with the imposed changes. Perry desisted again but allowed Reaves to go on with the idea if he wanted. Reaves did so and partnered with [[Maya Kaathryn Bohnhoff]] to write it. Meanwhile, Perry was approached by [[Shelly Shapiro]] to write [[W:c:indianajones:Indiana Jones and the Army of the Dead|''Indiana Jones and the Army of the Dead'']] for a [[2009]] release and accepted.<ref name="Perry Blog" />

There are conflicting reports whether ''Holostar'' was the novel's working title<ref name="padawans journal">{{WebCite|url=https://bookviewcafe.com/blog/2010/06/23/a-padawans-journal-entry-8-a-star-is-born%E2%80%94characters-and-where-they-come-from|text=A Padawan's Journal, Entry #8: A Star is Born—Characters and Where They Come From|author=Maya Kaathryn Bohnhoff|date=2010-06-23|work=Book View Cafe Blog|archivedate=20201004144547}}</ref> or not.<ref name="Perry Blog" /> Anyway, on [[October 4]], [[2010]], Del Rey announced that fans would get to choose the title of the novel. The three proposed titles were ''Star Wars: Shadow Games'', ''Star Wars: Pursuit'' and ''Star Wars: Shadow Play''.<ref name="you choose">{{Suvudu|subdomain=star-wars|url=2010/10/choose_next_star_wars_title.html|text=You Choose the Next Star Wars Title!|date=2010-10-04}}</ref> After a week, the title ''Star Wars: Shadow Games'' was chosen.<ref>{{Facebook|username=starwarsbooks|url=starwarsbooks/posts/158392457515332|name=Star Wars Books|date=2010-10-11|archivedate=20160117214904}}</ref> An exclusive Hardcover was released by the [[Science Fiction Book Club]].

